{"ref": "Mishnah Pesachim 10:6", "heRef": "משנה פסחים י׳:ו׳", "sectionRef": "Mishnah Pesachim 10", "indexTitle": "Mishnah Pesachim", "heIndexTitle": "משנה פסחים", "categories": ["Mishnah", "Seder Moed"], "next": null, "sectionNames": ["Chapter", "Mishnah"], "versions": [{"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Mishnah Yomit by Dr. Joshua Kulp", "license": "CC-BY", "versionSource": "http://learn.conservativeyeshiva.org/mishnah/", "text": "How far does one recite it? Bet Shammai say: Until “As a joyous mother of children” (Psalms 113:9). But Bet Hillel say: Until “The flinty rock into a fountain of waters” (Psalms 114:8). And he concludes with [a formula of] redemption. Rabbi Tarfon says: “Who redeemed us and redeemed our fathers from Egypt”, but he did not conclude [with a blessing]. Rabbi Akiva says: “So may the Lord our God and the God of our fathers bring us to other appointed times and festivals which come towards us for peace, rejoicing in the rebuilding of Your city and glad in Your service, and there we will eat of the sacrifices and the pesahim” etc. until “Blessed are You who has redeemed Israel.”"}], "available_versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Torat Emet 357", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "http://www.toratemetfreeware.com/index.html?downloads"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Mishnah, ed. Romm, Vilna 1913", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001741739"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "William Davidson Edition - English", "license": "CC-BY-NC", "versionSource": "https://korenpub.com/collections/the-noe-edition-koren-talmud-bavli-1"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Mishnah Yomit by Dr. Joshua Kulp", "license": "CC-BY", "versionSource": "http://learn.conservativeyeshiva.org/mishnah/"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "german", "actualLanguage": "de", "versionTitle": "Mischnajot mit deutscher Übersetzung und Erklärung. Berlin 1887-1933 [de]", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.talmud.de/tlmd/die-deutsche-mischna-uebersetzung"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "german", "actualLanguage": "de", "versionTitle": "Talmud Bavli. German. Lazarus Goldschmidt. 1929 [de]", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001042448/NLI"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Open Mishnah", "license": "CC-BY-SA", "versionSource": "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mishnah"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Sefaria Community Translation", "license": "CC0", "versionSource": "https://www.sefaria.org"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "The Mishna with Obadiah Bartenura by Rabbi Shraga Silverstein", "license": "CC-BY", "versionSource": "http://www.sefaria.org/shraga-silverstein"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "french", "actualLanguage": "fr", "versionTitle": "Le Talmud de Jérusalem, traduit par Moise Schwab, 1878-1890 [fr]", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002182155/NLI"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Mishnah based on the Kaufmann manuscript, edited by Dan Be'eri", "license": "PD", "versionSource": "https://archive.org/details/MishnaCorrectedKaufman00WHOLE"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "portuguese", "actualLanguage": "pt", "versionTitle": "Publicado em 5784, Saymon Pires da Silva [pt]", "license": "unknown", "versionSource": "Chavruta Chats Traduções"}]}